Rename ath9k_htc HTC protocol symbols to avoid qcacld-3.0 collision

The Qualcomm qca-wifi-host-cmn HTC module (built into this tree via
drivers/staging/qcacld-3.0) exports htc_init/htc_connect_service/
htc_send/htc_send_epid/htc_stop/htc_start/htc_sta_drain, which collide
with the identically named globals in drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/
htc_hst.c when CONFIG_ATH9K_HTC=y. Prefix the ath9k side with
ath9k_htc_hst_ so both USB Wi-Fi (AR9271) and the OnePlus onboard WLAN
can be built in.

This is required to enable the in-tree USB Wi-Fi drivers:
  CONFIG_ATH9K_HTC=y (AR9271), CONFIG_RT2800USB=y (RT3070/5370/5572),
  CONFIG_MT7601U=y, plus CONFIG_CARL9170/AR5523/RT2500USB/RT73USB/
  RTL8XXXU, with htc_9271.fw/rt2870.bin/mt7601u.bin embedded via
  CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE.
---
